content.text:
Yes, and you're most of the way there already: the post-course email has a `{{var:training_folder}}` slot fed by `config.dropboxFolder`. The problem is *where* that value lives: it's a **per-cohort** field, so today you'd paste the workbook URL into every cohort's JSON. But the materials URL only changes **quarterly, per course type**. Mismatched update frequencies: that's the whole friction.

## The elegant fix: resolve the workbook URL by course *type*, from one map

Instead of a per-cohort field, look the URL up from `config.type` (`CSPO`/`CSM`/`CSD`) against a single source-of-truth map you touch once a quarter.

**1. One map, in `course-config.ts`:**
```ts
// Current workbook URLs. Update once per quarter when the /materials/ slug rotates.
const WORKBOOK_URLS: Record<string, string> = {
  CSPO: "https://agilepainrelief.com/materials/cspo-2026-q3-2922d7dfb842132c/CSPO%20Workbook.pdf",
  // CSM:  "...", CSD: "..."  ← add as you move each course off Dropbox
};

export function deriveWorkbookUrl(config: CourseConfig): string {
  const url = config.workbookUrl ?? WORKBOOK_URLS[config.type];
  if (!url) throw new Error(`No workbook URL for course type ${config.type}`);
  return url;
}
```

**2. `send-course-email.ts`:** `training_folder: deriveWorkbookUrl(config)` instead of `config.dropboxFolder`, and drop `dropboxFolder` from the required-field check.

**3. Per-cohort JSONs:** delete `dropboxFolder` entirely. (I kept an optional `config.workbookUrl` escape hatch above so a one-off cohort can override without touching the map — no boolean, just present/absent.)

Net effect: rotating a quarter is **one line in one file**; every future cohort email of that type picks it up automatically. Retiring the `dropboxFolder` field also finishes the "move off Dropbox" job in the email path.

## Two things to flag

- **The URL must point at the PDF file, not the folder.** We chose bare files with no directory index, so `.../cspo-2026-q3-XXXX/` returns nothing usable: it has to be the full `...CSPO%20Workbook.pdf` link (note the `%20` for the space).
- **I'd keep the map full-URL, not slug + derived filename.** You can paste it straight from the browser, and it sidesteps filename-encoding logic. Slight base-URL repetition, but explicit and unbreakable.

I did *not* wire this to the Astro repo's `public/materials/` slug as a shared constant. It's tempting (one true slug), but `email-automation/` is a separate package that doesn't rebuild on site changes, so coupling them buys little and adds cross-package fragility.

Want me to implement this (map + `deriveWorkbookUrl` + swap in `send-course-email.ts` + strip `dropboxFolder` from the three JSONs)? I'll leave the diff ready for you to commit.

